// Build settings that are not Xcode's to own.
//
// The bundle id and the signing team are NOT here, deliberately. They live as literals in the
// pbxproj because Xcode rewrites them whenever Signing & Capabilities is touched in the UI, so a
// `$(VARIABLE)` in this file is overwritten within one session and the two then disagree silently.
// There is one app, one id and one team, so the shortest honest form wins:
//
//   dev.dubec.monad                  the app, simulator and device alike
//   dev.dubec.monad.CheckInWidget    the Live Activity extension, derived by hand
//   3D6D8LQ6F2                       DEVELOPMENT_TEAM — "Jakub Dubec (Personal Team)"
//
// An extension's id must be its host's plus one dot-separated suffix. Change the app's id and the
// widget's must change with it, or the device build fails to sign while the simulator keeps working.
//
// THE TEAM ID IS NOT THE STRING IN THE CERTIFICATE'S NAME. This repo carried that mistake for
// months, in a comment that told the next reader to copy the wrong value:
//
//   subject= CN=Apple Development: Jakub Dubec (GS862349S6), OU=3D6D8LQ6F2, O=Jakub Dubec
//                                                ^ cert id        ^ TEAM ID
//
// The parenthesised GS862349S6 is the certificate's own identifier. The Team ID is the OU. Read it
// with `security find-certificate -c "Apple Development: Jakub Dubec" -p | openssl x509 -noout
// -subject`, or from Xcode -> Settings -> Accounts beside the "(Personal Team)" row.
//
// `O=Jakub Dubec` also settles a second error this repo repeated: 3D6D8LQ6F2 was described as a
// PAID lab team distinct from a personal one. It is the personal team. There is only one, and
// there never was another.
//
// WHAT THIS BUILD CANNOT DO, because a free personal team can sign none of it
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// An entitlement a team cannot grant is a SIGNING failure, not a runtime one, so the entitlements
// file is an empty dict and these four are absent rather than requested:
//
//   aps-environment       No push, at all. The in-app inbox still works — it polls
//                         GET /api/me/notifications over HTTP and needs no entitlement. Live
//                         Activities are unaffected: this app starts and updates its own, which
//                         needs neither push nor an entitlement.
//   associated-domains    No Universal Links. Scanning a printed card with the CAMERA app opens
//                         Safari, which is why monad.dubec.dev/m/<code> must be a real page. The
//                         in-app scanner is unaffected.
//   HotspotConfiguration  Cannot join a Wi-Fi network itself. Irrelevant here: the AX210 fleet
//                         cannot be an access point, so there is none to join.
//   wifi-info             Cannot read back the SSID, so a session sidecar records an empty one.
//
// A free personal team's provisioning profile expires after SEVEN DAYS. The app stops launching on
// the eighth and needs a rebuild from Xcode.
APP_NAME = Monad Scan
OTHER_LDFLAGS = $(inherited) -lsqlite3
ENTITLEMENTS_FILE = iosApp/iosApp.entitlements
